WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.421
Week 13: City, Directions, and Public Services. ask for and give directions identify public services confirm a route

2
00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:15.092
Cultural lens. Urban grids, historic centers, public squares, addresses, and landmarks.

3
00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:27.526
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:39.533
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:48.746
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.746 --> 00:01:21.105
Model language. Muchas ciudades usan una cuadrícula de calles. — Many cities use a street grid. El centro histórico suele tener calles estrechas. — The historic center usually has narrow streets. Las direcciones a veces usan puntos de referencia. — Addresses sometimes use landmarks. El transporte urbano varía mucho entre ciudades. — Urban transport varies a lot between cities. Cada sistema funciona de forma distinta. — Each system works differently.

7
00:01:21.105 --> 00:01:31.259
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
